title: The War with Poland
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_poland_timer <= 0 and year = 1920 and month >= 5 and month <= 9 and warsaw_outcome = 0
on-arrival: c_poland_timer = 3; month_actions += 1
frequency: 300
is-card: true
tags: international

= The War with Poland

Piłsudski's armies marched on Kiev in the spring, and the Red Army has thrown them back. [? if month >= 7 : Now Tukhachevsky's cavalry is riding west towards Warsaw. ?] Munitions for Poland come through Germany, by rail from France and by sea through Hamburg and Danzig. The government has declared neutrality, and the right wonders aloud which side to march with.

- @block: Have the Hamburg dockers stop the munitions ships.
- @neutrality: Inspect every train, with the USPD and the unions.
- @prepare: Prepare to rise when the Red Army reaches the border.
- @easy_discard

@block
subtitle: The port stops, and Moscow hears of it. The Hamburg police will not let it pass.
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.district_hamburg_strike) {
    RG.startStrike('hamburg');
}
RG.district('hamburg', {repression: 6});
RG.ecci('lenin', 6);
Q.world_revolution += 3;
!}

The dockers find out what is in the crates and put down their hooks. The ship sails a week late, half empty.

@neutrality
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Workers' control of transit. Relations with the Independents improve.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The railwaymen's and transport workers' unions agree to inspect every train that crosses Germany. It is the first thing the union leaders have done for Soviet Russia.

@prepare
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The red guards grow, and so does the police's interest.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an uprising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.red_guards_strength += 1.5;
Q.repression += 6;
RG.ecci('bukharin', 5);
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

In East Prussia and Upper Silesia, our districts draw up lists of rail junctions and police stations. Everyone waits for news from Warsaw.
